// The SpiceDB analogue of fga.mod: the one file that has to know about every
// module, because SpiceDB has no `extend type`. `import` pulls each module's
// definitions and partials into one compile-time symbol table (verified: a
// module file does NOT need to `import` the other modules it references by
// name -- only this root file needs to reach all of them; see
// schema-mapping.md's "Modular models" section for how that was verified).
//
// `organization` itself is declared here, not in core.zed, because assembling
// it is the one piece of work that has no owner in the module structure: core
// owns organization's *base* shape, but can_create_space and can_create_project
// are owned by wiki and issue-tracker respectively, and nothing in OpenFGA's own
// module system requires core to know that either of them exists.
//
// This file is NOT what gets deployed, because it uses `import` across four
// files. `import` is rejected by a real SpiceDB WriteSchema unconditionally --
// verified live on v1.54.0 and v1.56.0, in both its bare form (as used here,
// "Unexpected token at root level") and its `use import`-flagged form ("import
// statements are not allowed in this context"). `zed validate` accepts this
// file's bare-keyword form directly (that is the "extended syntax" zed's own
// tooling understands), which is exactly why validating this file proves
// nothing about whether it can be deployed. Run
// `zed schema compile modules/manifest.zed --out schema.zed` to produce the
// file that actually gets written.
//
// Note this is specific to `import`, not to `partial` in general: a
// single-file schema using only `partial` (no `import`) CAN deploy directly
// via `use partial`, with no compile step -- verified live. See
// schema-mapping.md's "Modular models" section, "Three ways to ship a modular
// schema", for that option and why this store's artifacts use the compiled
// form instead.

import "./core.zed"
import "./wiki.zed"
import "./issue-tracker/projects.zed"
import "./issue-tracker/tickets.zed"

definition organization {
	...core_organization
	...wiki_organization_ext
	...issuetracker_organization_ext
}
